-- Plain MLM-USE. Same domain as USE/Vehicle.use, but restructured across
-- three levels of instantiation instead of one level of generalization:
--   Vehicle   (M3, most abstract -- defines wheels/isMultiTrack/PositiveWheels)
--   Car       (M2 -- its OWN seats/isFamilyCar/ReasonableSeats, AND
--              instantiates Vehicle, renaming "wheels" to "wheelCount" and
--              cancelling PositiveWheels for this edge)
--   CarModel  (M1, most concrete -- its OWN modelYear/ValidYear, AND
--              instantiates Car, inheriting everything Car has -- both its
--              own features and what Car itself inherited from Vehicle)
--
-- Things worth noticing when reading this (see the "defined vs. declared"
-- discussion this example came from):
--   - Operations are ALWAYS fully inherited through a clabject edge, with
--     no cancellation mechanism at all -- unlike attributes/roles/
--     constraints, which each get their own optional rename/removal
--     section in a clabject's body. isMultiTrack, defined once on Vehicle,
--     is simply callable on Car and CarModel alike.
--   - A clabject's rename/removal can only target something its DIRECT
--     parent (the one named right after ":") owns itself, not something
--     further up the chain. That's why "wheels -> wheelCount" and
--     "~PositiveWheels" are declared on the Car:Vehicle mediator, not the
--     CarModel:Car one, even though CarModel is the class you'd instantiate
--     in an object diagram.

MLM VehicleTaxonomy

model M3

class Vehicle
attributes
  wheels: Integer
operations
  isMultiTrack(): Boolean = self.wheels > 2
end

constraints
context Vehicle inv PositiveWheels:
  self.wheels > 0


model M2

class Car
attributes
  seats: Integer
operations
  isFamilyCar(): Boolean = self.seats >= 5
end

constraints
context Car inv ReasonableSeats:
  self.seats > 0 and self.seats <= 9


model M1

class CarModel
attributes
  modelYear: Integer
end

constraints
context CarModel inv ValidYear:
  self.modelYear > 1900


mediator M3 < NONE
end

mediator M2 < M3
clabject Car : Vehicle
attributes
wheels -> wheelCount
constraints
~PositiveWheels
end
end

mediator M1 < M2
clabject CarModel : Car
end
end
